// @emit-error an i32-keyed Map/Set is supported as a binding / parameter / return / `| null` / an ARRAY ELEMENT / a closure result / a map value
// CAPABILITY (B6b): the map as a UNION MEMBER, pinned at the REAL condition now
// that the FIELD position it used to hide behind is open.
//
// This is the sharp edge of `i32MapSpellingLowerable`'s new union arm. A union
// spelling reaches that gate as ONE `TypeRef`, and the arm accepts a member that
// is a struct ARM carrying the map in a FIELD (`{f: {[i32]: V}} | i32`, which
// `i32-keyed-variant-field.vl` runs) precisely because the field ROW now carries
// the key. A member that IS the map does not: a union member lowers into the
// shared BOX (`{tag, value}` with an `anyref` payload), and nothing in that box
// records which of the two map structs the payload holds — so the unbox at the
// `is`-narrowed read would `ref.cast` to whichever struct the member NAME scan
// happened to claim. The STRING-keyed twin of this program runs, so this is a
// position gate and not a value gate.
//
// The one-line difference from the accepted form is the absence of a field name:
//   `{f: {[i32]: i32}} | i32`   accepted — the map is a FIELD of an arm
//   `{[i32]: i32} | i32`        this file — the map IS the arm
const m: {[i32]: i32} = Map()
m[1] = 7
const u: {[i32]: i32} | i32 = m
if u is {[i32]: i32} {
  print(u.length)
} else {
  print(-1)
}
